      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Experienced the issue on Quest 2, and I have someone who claims to experience it on PC as well but I've yet to reproduce the issue on PC.\n\nI found the issue was tied to the complexity of my map mesh when using mesh colliders.\n\nI made a room in Blender, subdivided until I had 100k vertices, and then brought it into Unity as a mesh collider. Then whenever I picked up a trigger collider while in the room, I lagged. Standing still with the trigger collider in my hand would improve my fps, but shaking the pickup brought me to a slideshow\n\nI didn't notice any log spam",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "63bfaf2231665e72177bd872",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5ae0cfe99d21e660db186ece",
