      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was able to recreate the issue on Desktop as well.\n\nYou need around a lot of vertices in a mesh collider and your trigger pickup has to be inside the bounding box of the mesh collider. I was able to reproduce the lag with 1M vertices\n\nNon-trigger colliders still don't cause any performance issues so we know that Unity is capable of calculating collisions with high poly mesh colliders pretty efficiently. I had always assumed that trigger colliders were more efficient than non-trigger colliders but maybe that assumption is just wrong",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
